Record a full block's best posting before flushing the block

Applies to vchord_bm25 0.3.0 (upstream tag 0.3.0, commit c610b7ab).

InvertedSerializer::write builds a term's posting list when an index is built
over existing rows: CREATE INDEX, CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY, REINDEX. For each
posting it first checks whether the posting ends the current 128-posting block
and flushes the block with the running best (blockwand_tf and
blockwand_fieldnorm_id). Only then does it check whether the posting is the
block's best and record it. So when a block's best posting is its last one,
the block is flushed with the previous block's best, or with 0 for a leading
run of such blocks. Ties make that common: FixedBlockPartition picks the best
with `max_by`, which returns the last of equal maxima.

A bounded scan (finite bm25_catalog.bm25_limit) skips a block whose summary is
below its threshold, so it drops postings that belong in the top-k. The exact
scan does not read the summaries. The insert and seal path (append.rs) updates
the running best before it flushes and is unaffected.

The fix records the best posting before the flush check. It changes no on-disk
format and no SQL.

Measured, against the same SQL:
- 300 identical rows, REINDEX, bounded top-90: 44 rows unpatched, 90 patched.
- 20,000-document random corpus, CREATE INDEX: 14 of the 1,227 terms with at
  least 128 postings had a worse bounded top-90 unpatched (1,228 ranks); none
  patched.

License: this patch modifies vchord_bm25 and is offered under the same terms
as vchord_bm25 itself: AGPL-3.0-only or Elastic-2.0, at the recipient's option.
---
diff --git a/src/segment/posting/serializer.rs b/src/segment/posting/serializer.rs
index 9278d3e..0b8f8f8 100644
--- a/src/segment/posting/serializer.rs
+++ b/src/segment/posting/serializer.rs
@@ -85,15 +85,15 @@ impl<R: FieldNormRead> InvertedWrite for InvertedSerializer<R> {
         self.postings_serializer.new_term();
         for (i, (doc_id, freq)) in recorder.iter().enumerate() {
             self.postings_serializer.write_doc(doc_id, freq);
+            if max_doc.get(block_count).copied() == Some(i as u32) {
+                blockwand_tf = freq;
+                blockwand_fieldnorm_id = self.fieldnorm_reader.read(doc_id);
+            }
             if partitions.get(block_count).copied() == Some(i as u32) {
                 self.postings_serializer
                     .flush_block(blockwand_tf, blockwand_fieldnorm_id);
                 block_count += 1;
             }
-            if max_doc.get(block_count).copied() == Some(i as u32) {
-                blockwand_tf = freq;
-                blockwand_fieldnorm_id = self.fieldnorm_reader.read(doc_id);
-            }
         }
         assert!(block_count == partitions.len());
         self.block_partition.reset();
